-- title:
--   Base change of the j-finite Igusa chart to a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $N\ge 1$ an integer with $p\nmid N$, and write $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb Q$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $K'$ be an intermediate field of $L(\!(q)\!)$ over $L$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 (N*p)))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise images under `coeffEmb L` of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(Np)$ over $\mathbb Q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over $L$ making $L$ a fraction field of $A$, carrying a $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$-algebra structure compatible with that of $L$, and such that the image of $p$ in $A$ lies in the maximal ideal; assume $A$ acts on $K'$ through $L$. Let $j'\in K'$ be non-zero with underlying Laurent series the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb L jq` of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } jNumQ)$ of the modular invariant. Then there is an isomorphism of $A$-algebras $$e\colon A\otimes_{\mathbb Z_{(p)}}\ \mathrm{chartAlgFin}(Np,p)\ \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\ \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin}\,A\,K'\,j',$$ where the source factor is the subalgebra of elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull (N*p)` integral over $\mathbb Z_{(p)}[j]$ and the target is the subalgebra of elements of $K'$ integral over $A[j']$, with the property that for every $b$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}(Np,p)$ the Laurent series in $L(\!(q)\!)$ underlying $e(1\otimes b)$ is the coefficientwise image under `coeffEmb L` of the Laurent series underlying $b$.
--
--   This identifies the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model attached to the $q$-expansion function field of $X_0(Np)$ over an arbitrary discrete valuation ring $A$ of residue characteristic $p$ with the base change along $\mathbb Z_{(p)}\to A$ of the corresponding chart of the Igusa scheme at level $Np$, compatibly with $q$-expansions. It is used in the analysis of the $j$-chart of the full-level model, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgFin_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgFin_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul), where the number of minimal primes over $p$ in these chart rings is read off.
